        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Hydration examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert, mildly irritable, ambulant and in no acute distress. Oral mucosa dry with mild thirst; skin turgor slightly decreased at sternum; capillary refill under 2 seconds; no peripheral oedema. Findings documented as consistent with mild–moderate dehydration."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Back examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Normal inspection with no deformity or bruising. Bilateral paraspinal muscle tenderness at L3–L5; no midline bony tenderness. Full range of motion, uncomfortable especially with extension; pain reproducible with lumbar extension and prolonged standing. Straight leg raise negative bilaterally."
      }
    },
